\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. How happy are they
\par Who the Saviour obey,
\par And have laid up their treasure above.
\par Tongue cannot express
\par The sweet comfort and peace
\par Of a soul in its earliest love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. That comfort was mine,
\par When the favour divine
\par I first found in the blood of the Lamb;
\par When my heart it believed,
\par What a joy it received,
\par What a heaven in Jesus's name!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Jesus all the day long
\par Was my joy and my song;
\par O that all His salvation may see!
\par He hath loved me, I cried;
\par He hath suffered, and died,
\par To redeem such a rebel as me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O the rapturous height
\par Of the holy delight
\par Which I felt in the life-giving blood!
\par Of my Saviour possessed
\par I was perfectly blessed
\par As if  filled with the fullness of God.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

